      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Steven pays per room by the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned. This can be represented by the following equation:\n\n$\\text{Total amount owed} = \\text{Amount paid per room} \\times \\text{Number of rooms cleaned}$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have:\n\n$\\text{Total amount owed} = \\dfrac{11}{2} \\times \\dfrac{7}{3}$\n\nMultiplying the numerators and denominators, we get:\n\n$\\text{Total amount owed} = \\dfrac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\dfrac{77}{6}$\n\nTherefore, Steven owes Jeremy $\\boxed{\\dfrac{77}{6}}$ dollars.",
