    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned by the rate at which Steven pays. The rate is $\\frac{11}{2}$ dollars per room, and Jeremy cleaned $\\frac{7}{3}$ rooms. Therefore, the total amount Steven owes Jeremy is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\nTo multiply these fractions, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\frac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{77}{6}\n\\]\n\nThus, Steven owes Jeremy $\\frac{77}{6}$ dollars. The final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{77}{6}}\n\\]",
